# A RESOLVE LINE NAMING SOMETHING ALREADY DECIDED. The rule answers the citation, so its finding is a
# proposed edit; the line beneath it answers a question nobody asked. A resolution is legal only against
# an unresolved finding — against anything else it is an input that was meant to mean something, and the
# run refuses rather than riding along.
rule cite DESIGN 4b => gunbc.reference_migration_unresolved_citer::reference_migration_unresolved_citer_value
resolve fixtures/reference_migration_refused/dag/gunbc/reference_migration_unresolved_citer.dag@437-446 6c59bd538cd85e424ba55c108950475a930211f5a82984509b832b82eb34ffda => gunbc.reference_migration_unresolved_citer::reference_migration_unresolved_citer_value
